1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,981
Meet Abu Salim. His date palms have stood on this farm for forty years.

2
00:00:08,331 --> 00:00:10,827
Abu Salim: Another season... and still no dates.

3
00:00:12,433 --> 00:00:17,553
Abu Salim: I cut them down. But now what? I can't sell them, and I can't just burn them.

4
00:00:17,903 --> 00:00:19,780
Heavy trunks, and nowhere to go.

5
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,347
ARIBS driver: Assalamu Alaikum, Abu Salim! Leave those trunks to us.

6
00:00:25,697 --> 00:00:28,043
ARIBS collects them, right from his farm.

7
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:34,472
At our factory in Barka, palm trunks go in... and natural palm peat comes out.

8
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:43,192
Packed in sealed two-hundred-litre bags, or supplied loose, by the kilo or the ton.

9
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,928
ARIBS driver: Abu Salim! Remember your old palms? They're back!

10
00:00:50,278 --> 00:00:51,963
Abu Salim: Welcome back, my friends!

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,672
Mixed into the soil, palm peat holds water longer, so every drop goes further.

12
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,624
Abu Salim: Look at this! Tomatoes, peppers... my farm is alive again.

13
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,080
Abu Salim: Shukran, ARIBS!

14
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:18,550
From burden to better soil. ARIBS, helping make Oman greener, one palm at a time.
